\title{HrankdCov: Distribution-free tests of multivariate independence}
\description{
Center-outward ranks and signs (Hallin et al., 2021) extend univariate
ranks to random vectors through optimal transport of the data onto a
regular grid in the unit ball.  This package computes them and uses them
in the distance covariance to obtain tests of independence between two
random vectors that are both distribution-free and consistent (Shi,
Drton and Han, 2022; Shi, Hallin, Drton and Han, 2022).
}
\details{
Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=hrank_dcov_test]{hrank_dcov_test()}}: the test of independence;
\item \code{\link[=hrank_dcov]{hrank_dcov()}}: the test statistic;
\item \code{\link[=hrank_dcov_null]{hrank_dcov_null()}}: its distribution-free null distribution, for reuse
across many tests;
\item \code{\link[=co_ranks]{co_ranks()}}, \code{\link[=co_grid]{co_grid()}}, \code{\link[=co_scores]{co_scores()}}: center-outward ranks, signs,
grids and scores.
}

See \code{vignette("HrankdCov")} for an introduction.
}
